Title: Judge's X Word Puzzle No. 6
Author: Catherine McMillan
Date: 1927-06-04
Byline: Submitted by Catherine McMillan, Chicago, Ill. Judge will pay $10 for each puzzle printed.
Source: https://archive.org/details/sim_judge_1927-06-04_92/page/n32/mode/1up
Number: 6
Solution-Source: https://archive.org/details/sim_judge_1927-06-11_92/page/n32/mode/1up


##PARTY#BACON##
#NATURE#EVADES#
CAREFUL#CONDUCT
APT#FELLOWS#TOW
SKAT#ROOMS#ERNE
TIKES#WOE#PLACE
SNEAKY#S#SEALED
###MURDERERS###
STAINS#N#ACTUAL
TRUNK#YES#HINGE
RING#VESTS#CARE
ACT#REASONS#RED
POISONS#VOLUMES
#TEAPOT#ERASED#
##STEMS#SEWED##


A1. Name a social gathering that is usually "all wet." ~ PARTY
A6. Name something that is always on the hog. ~ BACON
A11. Who imposed a system of laws which cannot be repealed by any nation? ~ NATURE
A12. What does a Chicago gunman do to the police? ~ EVADES
A14. What kind of man is a misogamist? ~ CAREFUL
A15. What is supposed to be wrong with the younger generation? ~ CONDUCT
A17. What is a synonym for suitable? ~ APT
A18. What is another name for companions; pardners? ~ FELLOWS
A20. Name something that has a lot of pull. ~ TOW
A21. What would you say if you didn't want to feed the kitty? ~ SKAT
A23. Name things which always have baths in the best hotels. ~ ROOMS
A24. What eagle is found in many crossword puzzles? ~ ERNE
A25. What does Mother call the kids? ~ TIKES
A27. What will have to be dispelled before you can find the Bluebird? ~ WOE
A28. What is hard for a parking autoist to find? ~ PLACE
A29. What kind of men make good Federal agents? ~ SNEAKY
A31. What kind of package is "fastened securely"? ~ SEALED
A32. What kind of people form a considerable part of the population of Chicago? ~ MURDERERS
A33. What are blots on the escutcheon? ~ STAINS
A36. Name an adjective which means "acting or existing really and objectively." ~ ACTUAL
A40. What do a great many people who go to New York City live in? ~ TRUNK
A41. What little feminine affirmative causes all the trouble? ~ YES
A43. Name an object which is something to-a-door. ~ HINGE
A44. What ornament has an engaging look? ~ RING
A45. Name something that has no arms. (Plural) ~ VESTS
A47. Name something that should be taken when you cross the street. ~ CARE
A48. What do most actors do during their off hours? ~ ACT
A49. What is it that is so hard to get in explanation of the Eighteenth Amendment? ~ REASONS
A51. What color seems to excite Sect. Kellogg? ~ RED
A52. In what was Lucretia Borgia a specialist? ~ POISONS
A54. What are usually put on the shelf and left there? ~ VOLUMES
A56. Name a vessel which is just as useful on dry land as at sea. ~ TEAPOT
A57. Give a synonym for effaced. ~ ERASED
A58. What is very much attached to peaches? ~ STEMS
A59. What should the 9th hole be? ~ SEWED

D1. What do Federal agents do to a glass of liquor? ~ PARTAKE
D2. What did the guests do at Banquo's feast? ~ ATE
D3. What did Pierrot wear around his neck? ~ RUFF
D4. What was it impossible for Romeo to be to Juliet? ~ TRUER
D5. What is a race across the Pacific? ~ YELLOW
D6. What is a verb meaning "to grow or develop into"? ~ BECOME
D7. What does the swain do about his love? ~ AVOWS
D8. Name something manufactured in Detroit. ~ CANS
D9. What is an eccentric fellow? ~ ODD
D10. What kind of person is said to be "on the fence"? ~ NEUTRAL
D11. What is it that even married men can hold in their laps with impunity? ~ NAPKIN
D13. Name a wall ornament. ~ SCONCE
D14. What does a fisherman do to catch the poor fish? ~ CASTS
D16. What is the name of a twilled, woolen fabric? ~ TWEED
D19. What does a car-rattle signify? ~ LOOSENESS
D22. What was the probable former occupation of chauffeurs? ~ TEAMING
D24. What is it that always has a lot of pull? ~ ELASTIC
D26. Name a very unpopular animal? ~ SKUNK
D28. Name something that usually gets fried on Friday. ~ PERCH
D30. What is difficult for the girls to count? (abbr.) ~ YRS
D31. Where did the permanent waves originate? ~ SEA
D33. What is an early educator? ~ STRAP
D34. What is the name of a hand-knitted woolen yarn fabric? ~ TRICOT
D35. Who are the feminine relatives who often spoil the kids? ~ AUNTIES
D37. In what way is it dangerous to go around Chicago? ~ UNARMED
D38. What is it Mr. and Mrs. rarely ever did? ~ AGREED
D39. What English duke was Lord Treasurer and spent five years in prison? ~ LEEDS
D41. What little things cause many an uprising? ~ YEASTS
D42. What are useless unless they're kept hot? (Plural) ~ STOVES
D45. What is the dangerous thing about a rattlesnake? ~ VENOM
D46. What is one thing sheet-music is made from? ~ SNORE
D49. What do some people who go in the cigar business seem to have a lot of? ~ ROPE
D50. What does many a cabbage-head come to? ~ SLAW
D53. What did Little Jack Horner do in the corner? ~ SAT
D55. What word means application; employment? ~ USE


